<title>USA: List of Florida towns, districts in fiscal trouble.</title>
<headline>List of Florida towns, districts in fiscal trouble.</headline>
<dateline>TALLAHASSEE, Fla 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following Florida cities and service districts are deemed by the state auditor general to be in a state of &quot;financial emergency.&quot;:</p>
<p>City of Alachua</p>
<p>City of Bowling Green</p>
<p>Town of Horseshoe Beach</p>
<p>Town of Noma</p>
<p>Town of Westville</p>
<p>Aucilla Area Solid Waste Administration District</p>
<p>Baker County Hospital Authority</p>
<p>Braden River Fire Control and Rescue District</p>
<p>Dunes Community Development District</p>
<p>Lanark Village Water and Sewer District</p>
<p>Ocean Highway and Port Authority of Nassau County</p>
<p>Orange County Research and Development Authority</p>
<p>Orlando-Orange County Expressway Authority</p>
<p>Pinellas Suncoast Transit Authority</p>
<p>Reserve Community Development District</p>
<p>St. Lucie West Services District</p>
<p>Village Center Community Development District</p>
<p>These Florida cities and service districts &quot;may be in a state of financial emergency,&quot; according to the state auditor:</p>
<p>City of Cape Coral</p>
<p>City of Crestview</p>
<p>Town of Cross City</p>
<p>City of Crystal River</p>
<p>Village of Highland Park</p>
<p>Town of Inglis</p>
<p>Town of Jennings</p>
<p>City of Miami</p>
<p>City of Mullberry</p>
<p>City of Pahokee</p>
<p>Town of Penney Farms</p>
<p>Town of Ponce De Leon</p>
<p>Village of Royal Palm Beach</p>
<p>Town of Sneads</p>
<p>City of South Bay.</p>
<p>City of St. Augustine</p>
<p>City of Tamarac</p>
<p>City of Waldo</p>
<p>Town of White Springs</p>
<p>Acme Improvement District</p>
<p>Cedar Key Special Water and Sewerage District</p>
<p>Enterprise Community Development District</p>
<p>Gateway Services District</p>
<p>Performing Arts Center Authority</p>
<p>Solid Waste Authority of Palm Beach County.</p>
<p>Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
</text>
